l-1 trauma centre at CHU Grenoble Alpes, with CHU Chambery the other regional referral. The emergency number is 112. (Source: https://www.ch-bsm.fr/urgences.html and https://www.chu-grenoble.fr/patients-et-accompagnants/offre-de-soin/urgences-adultes-nord - accessed 2026-08-06.)","source":"https://www.ch-bsm.fr/urgences.html","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"When is the best time to ski Val d''Isere?","a":"The core winter season runs late November to early May - the official 2026-27 dates are 28 November 2026 to 2 May 2027 - plus a summer glacier season on the Pissaillas roughly early July to late August. High terrain (village 1,850 m, lifts to about 3,197 m on the Pissaillas glacier and about 3,456 m area-wide at the Grande Motte) makes snow relatively reliable, but exact opening and closing shift with conditions. (Source: https://www.valdisere.com/en/val-disere/faq/ and https://www.seevaldisere.com/lifts/dates - accessed 2026-08-06; verify before travel.)","source":"https://www.valdisere.com/en/val-disere/faq/","si_tag":"ski"},{"q":"How much is a Val d''Isere lift pass?","a":"For winter 2025-26 the Tignes-Val d''Isere full-area adult pass is about EUR 75 for one day and EUR 450 for six days (ages 19-64); it is cheaper early and late season and is effectively dynamic by date. 2026-27 prices were not published as of August 2026. (Source: https://www.seevaldisere.com/ski-passes/ and https://www.valdisere.com/en/prepare-for-your-stay/buy-my-skipass/ - accessed 2026-08-06; verify before travel.)","source":"https://www.seevaldisere.com/ski-passes/","si_tag":"ski"},{"q":"Is Val d''Isere good for beginners?","a":"For progression yes, with a caveat: the linked Tignes-Val d''Isere area is about 300 km of piste with green and blue runs and ski schools, but much of Val d''Isere''s own terrain is red and black and the village home runs can be demanding, so beginners are usually pointed to the La Daille and Solaise nursery areas. (Source: https://www.valdisere.com/en/val-disere/faq/ - the ''I am a beginner, where should I go to ski?'' entry - accessed 2026-08-06.)","source":"https://www.valdisere.com/en/val-disere/faq/","si_tag":"ski"},{"q":"Val d''Isere or Tignes - which, and how do I get there?","a":"They share one 300 km linked ski area (historically l''Espace Killy, now marketed as Tignes-Val d''Isere) on a single pass, so the choice is base-village character rather than terrain. Nearest airports are Geneva, Lyon and Chambery with a roughly 2.5-3.5 hour transfer; the nearest railway station is Bourg-Saint-Maurice, about 30 km away, with an onward bus or transfer. (Source: https://www.valdisere.com/en/val-disere/faq/ and https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tignes_%E2%80%93_Val_d%27Isere - accessed 2026-08-06.)","source":"https://www.valdisere.com/en/val-disere/faq/","si_tag":"ski"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Val d''Isere Travel Guide: Snow-Sure Skiing, the Espace Killy & World Cup Racing","meta_description":"Plan Val d''Isere — the snow-sure Tarentaise resort at 1,850 m: the 300 km Espace Killy linked with Tignes, the Olympic Face de Bellevarde and Criterium de la Premiere Neige World Cup, legendary off-piste, snow-front five-star palaces and the Vanoise National Park, with real timing, safety and booking intel.","slug":"val-d-isere-france","primary_keyword":"Val d''Isere travel guide","long_tail":["Val d''Isere ski season dates","Espace Killy Tignes Val d''Isere piste map","Face de Bellevarde","Criterium de la Premiere Neige World Cup","Val d''Isere off-piste","Val d''Isere luxury hotels"],"search_language":"fr","local_keywords":["Val d''Isere guide de voyage","domaine skiable Espace Killy Tignes","Face de Bellevarde","Criterium de la Premiere Neige","hors-piste Val d''Isere","hotels de luxe Val d''Isere","Parc national de la Vanoise"],"hreflang":["en","fr-FR"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-17","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-07-17","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/france","read":"2026-08-20T14:48:26Z","source_updated":"2026-08-11T10:17:02+01:00"}]}},"booking":{"codes":["terrorism","civil-unrest","petty-crime"],"advisory_updated":"accessed 2026-07-17)","note":"concerns are urban terrorism/protests/pickpocketing — in-resort the main risk is the alpine environment, not security"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"ski","status":"live"},{"si":"adventure","status":"future"},{"si":"Sports Travel","status":"future"},{"si":"Luxury / Ultra-Luxury","status":"future"},{"si":"Apres-ski & Nightlife","status":"future"},{"si":"romance","status":"live"},{"si":"wellness","status":"future"},{"si":"Hiking & Outdoor","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Airelles Val d''Isere","why_ultra":"snow-front Airelles five-star in the village centre, 1,200 m2 Guerlain spa, four restaurants, children''s kingdom","earning":"consortia/Virtuoso on application","virtuoso_value_add":true,"mor":"commissionable-rack","tier":"ultra","price_band":"~EUR 900-3,500/night (approx; suites + peak higher)"},{"name":"Les Barmes de l''Ours","why_ultra":"iconic slopeside five-star at the foot of Bellevarde, 49 rooms + 27 suites, 1,000 m2 spa","earning":"consortia/Virtuoso on application","virtuoso_value_add":true,"mor":"commissionable-rack","tier":"ultra","price_band":"~EUR 700-2,800/night (approx)"},{"name":"Le K2 Chogori","why_ultra":"intimate contemporary K2 Collection five-star (opened Dec 2020), 21 rooms/suites over ~3,000 m2, Goji Spa","earning":"consortia/on application","virtuoso_value_add":true,"mor":"commissionable-rack","tier":"ultra","price_band":"~EUR 800-3,000/night (approx)"},{"name":"Le Refuge de Solaise","why_ultra":"five-star mountaintop hotel at 2,551 m, ski-in eyrie reached only by ski or gondola, pool + spa","earning":"consortia/on application","virtuoso_value_add":true,"mor":"commissionable-rack","tier":"luxury","price_band":"~EUR 600-2,500/night (approx)"},{"name":"Criterium World Cup private hospitality + palace suite + catered chalet","why_ultra":"exclusive-use World Cup weekend + private chalet base for groups","earning":"DMC/event packaging + chalet specialists","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"hospitality + chalet on application (approx)"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-17","hero":{"query":"Val d''Isère, France"},"geo":{"lat":45.4489,"lng":6.9797},"orbit":[{"id":"alpe-dhuez-france","jewels":35,"si":["ski","family","ultra","entertainment","wellness","romance"]},{"id":"chamonix-france","jewels":23,"si":["ski","adventure","hiking","ultra","romance","culture","wellness"]},{"id":"courchevel-france","jewels":23,"si":["ski","ultra","culinary","romance","wellness","family"]},{"id":"la-plagne-france","jewels":34,"si":["ski","family","adventure","wellness","ultra","romance"]},{"id":"les-deux-alpes-france","jewels":34,"si":["ski","adventure","entertainment","family","wellness","romance"]},{"id":"megeve-france","jewels":33,"si":["ski","ultra","culinary","romance","wellness","family"]},{"id":"meribel-france","jewels":28,"si":["ski","family","romance","ultra","hiking","wellness","culinary"]},{"id":"tignes-france","jewels":24,"si":["ski","family","hiking","wellness","ultra","entertainment"]},{"id":"val-thorens-france","jewels":32,"si":["ski","ultra","culinary","family","wellness","romance"]}],"orbit_country":["aix-en-provence-france","alsace-france","amboise-france","antibes-france","arles-france","auvers-sur-oise-france","avignon-france","barbizon-france","bayeux-d-day-france","cannes-france","cassis-france","chantilly-france","disneyland-paris-france","dordogne-france","etretat-france","fontainebleau-france","french-riviera","giverny-france","gordes-luberon-france","honfleur-france","iles-de-lerins-france","loire-valley-france","marseille-france","menton-france","mont-saint-michel-france","nice-france","normandy-france","paris-france","provence-france","provins-france","rambouillet-france","rouen-france","saint-germain-en-laye-france","saint-tropez-france","senlis-france","vaux-le-vicomte-france","versailles-france"]}'::jsonb, 121),
  ('val-thorens-france', '01F', 'Val Thorens', 'France', 'The highest resort in Europe', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'French Alps', '{"ski","ultra","culinary","family","wellness","romance"}', '{"alpine","dramatic","adventurous"}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["The HIGHEST ski resort in Europe — village ~2,300 m; ski area 1,825-3,230 m (Pointe du Bouchet); Cime Caron cable car ~3,200 m","Gateway to Les 3 Vallees — world''s largest linked ski area: 600 km slopes + 50 km ski routes, ~159 lifts (independent measure ~493 km - flag); own domain ~150 km","Snow-sure by altitude (entire resort above 1,800 m + glacier-fed high terrain); season ~mid-Nov to early May (3V 21 Nov 2026-2 May 2027)","Three 5-star hotels at 2,300 m: Pashmina - Le Refuge (L''OCCITANE spa), Altapura (Casa Alta), Koh-I Nor (800 m2 spa, two pools)","Michelin-level dining: Les Explorateurs (Pashmina, Michelin-billed) + Casa Alta (Altapura, Michelin star 2025) - confirm current stars","Les 3 Vallees adult DAY ticket EUR 81.80 (child 67) current season; 6-day + VT-only prices unverified; US pass (Ikon) NOT confirmed - do not assert","Europe''s most famous high-altitude open-air apres; Moutiers the rail gateway (~37 km/45min-1h up the Belleville valley)","HELI-SKIING BANNED IN FRANCE (1985) - guided off-piste/ski-touring only; NO natural hot springs (nearest thermal towns Brides-les-Bains/La Lechere down-valley - verify)"],"safety":{"emergency":"112 (Europe) / 15 SAMU / 17 police / 18 fire / 114 SMS; mountain rescue via 112 / PGHM (Tarentaise units Bourg-Saint-Maurice/Modane)","hospital":"Resort clinic; valley hospitals Moutiers / Albertville (CHAM); trauma Chambery / Grenoble / Annecy; heli evac SMUR/PGHM (verify facilities)","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"High-alpine winter sports at extreme altitude (village 2,300 m, top 3,230 m): off-piste avalanche risk - Meteo-France BERA, 5-level scale, Vanoise massif (verify Vanoise vs Haute-Tarentaise); transceiver/shovel/probe + UIAGM guide; NO heli-skiing (banned in France) - guided touring only; glacier/crevasse terrain guided; altitude (AMS possible on rapid ascent), severe cold/wind/whiteout; cat-3/4 sun protection; rescue 112/PGHM","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/france","read":"2026-08-20T14:48:26Z","page_updated":"2026-08-11T10:17:02+01:00","source_country":"france","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely"},"timing":{"peak":"High winter — Christmas/New Year, February European half-terms + Easter; 5-star + ski-in multiples + min-stay","shoulder":"Late Nov-mid Dec (snow-sure early opening) + Apr-early May spring skiing","green":"May-Nov closure (winter-dominant; no summer glacier skiing since ~2002; small summer hike/bike offer)","booking_lead":"Christmas/NY + Feb + Easter + top 5-stars/ski-in apartments 4-8 mo; regular winter 2-4 mo; spring-ski 1-3 mo","off_season_specials":"Snow-sure early-season (late Nov-mid Dec) + spring (Apr-May) value windows - ''great snow when others have none''","event_peaks":"Christmas/NY, Feb half-terms, Easter + season-opening/apres events (dates verify)","fire_date":"Next winter + 5-star suites/ski-in apartments from prior spring (4-8 mo); early-season from October; spring value from January; lead with ''highest resort in Europe / surest snow''"},"jewels":[{"name":"Ski the whole Trois Vallees - 600 km on one pass","si_tag":"Winter/Ski","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"adult day ~EUR 81.80; instructor ~350-650/day","timing":"ski mid-Nov-early May","draw_rank":1,"hook":"from the highest resort in Europe, drop into the world''s largest linked ski area and string Val Thorens, Méribel and Courchevel across a week","si":"ski","blurb":"from the highest resort in Europe, drop into the world''s largest linked ski area and string Val Thorens, Méribe